@label "Update integration"
@description "Update an integration row by id within the current account (ctx); the handler always stamps updatedAt. Every mutable column is a DECLARED PARAMETER and Nothing leaves it unchanged, so the signature IS the allowlist: `id`, `type`, `accountId` and `createdAt` are not things a caller can name. Returns Maybe<updated row>. Backs dashboard PUT /integrations/:id."
@tags "state" "io" "integration" "ts-elimination" "rights"
@ioAction "state.update_integration"
@requires "HasStateIO"
@native
-- ⚠ rights R4a C1a §0.5 — THE SIGNATURE IS THE FENCE, AND THE OLD ONE WAS A LIE.
--
-- This read `(id: String) -> (patch: {  }) -> Maybe ({  })`, and a
-- declared-empty record is what `AGENTS.md` names outright as a lie: "A
-- declared-empty record (`{ $record: { fields: [] } }` as a return, parameter or
-- field type) is a lie: the editor and inference take it as the real type." An undeclared
-- blob parameter is exactly what a raw `...patch` spread is FOR, and the handler
-- duly spread it into the SQL `SET` behind an `as never` cast that silenced the
-- one compiler error that would have caught it. Measured: a member OR a viewer
-- moved an owned integration — and its known secret — into another account with
-- `patch: { accountId: B }`.
--
-- C0b shipped a TypeScript allowlist to close that today, regen-free. This is
-- the real repair: with the five mutable columns declared as parameters, there
-- is no slot for `accountId` at all, so the forgery is UNREPRESENTABLE rather
-- than FILTERED, and the C0b allowlist is deleted in the same commit.
--
-- ⚠ THE RETURN IS STILL `Maybe ({  })` and that is still a declared-empty
-- record. It is honest to say so: the handler returns the whole row, and
-- declaring it would need an `IntegrationRow` type that does not exist (the
-- `Integration` entity in `fenel/std/entities/integration.fenel` is the AUTHORING
-- shape — no id, no accountId, no status, no timestamps). It is one of the
-- `empty-record-placeholders` the audit already counts, and it is not this
-- phase's.
updateIntegration : (id: String) -> (label: Maybe String) -> (credentials: Maybe ({  })) -> (config: Maybe ({  })) -> (status: Maybe String) -> (enabled: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe ({  })

